A solitary figure in traditional meditation posture sits atop a mountain peak at twilight, rendered in Vincent van Gogh's distinctive swirling brushstroke style. The sky above erupts in spiraling cosmic patterns of deep indigo, gold, and luminous teal, with stars and nebulae merging seamlessly into the surrounding landscape. The meditator's form dissolves at the edges, their robes blending into the mountainside below while their upper body seems to merge with the swirling heavens above. Cypress-like trees frame the scene, their forms echoing the cosmic spirals. The boundary between earth and sky, figure and universe, becomes deliberately ambiguous—rocks flow upward into starlight, celestial bodies cascade downward into terrain. Thick impasto texture throughout creates movement and energy, suggesting that stillness and cosmic motion are one unified expression.
